["er.request/1",{"definition_version":1,"fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"intent":{"causation":null,"command_id":"cmd-child-ad5bb48ece8bbb9d560ff9a5fae58a028971bd037819cb61f2070e9d21b49f9e","command_type":"aep.entity.create/v1","correlation_id":"protocol-artifact-new","execution_id":null,"expected_revision":null,"payload":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"## Outcome\n\nThe eventlog and entity-runtime tree stores carry no home path inside hex-encoded legacy bytes,\nas the four stores exported after aep#23 do not.\n\n## Why\n\nThose two stores were exported before the export rewrote inside hex. Their legacy provenance\nblobs still decode to home-relative paths (the tilde form) (entity-runtime: 428 occurrences; eventlog not counted),\nthe same bytes their `aep.project/2` history already holds, and no names. `validate` S9 does not\ndecode hex, so it does not see them.\n\n## Open question\n\nA tree store's history files are immutable (V2), so removing them means either a second export\nthat replays the writes made since the cutover, or a store-level rewrite verb. Neither exists.\n","status":"draft","title":"The two trees exported before the hex rewrite carry no home path in their legacy bytes"},"entity_type":"aep.story/v1","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/early-tree-exports-carry-no-home-path-in-legacy-hex"},"target":null,"task":null},"result":{"affected":["ent-772b054de23fdbd47637effbf92420a1@1"],"audit":["aud-85c435504e9044e6e6155dbfa7c133a9"],"command_id":"cmd-child-ad5bb48ece8bbb9d560ff9a5fae58a028971bd037819cb61f2070e9d21b49f9e","consistency":"seq-000000000000","events":["evt-85c434504e904333e6155abfa7c12e90"],"outcome":"accepted"}},"lifecycle_state":"recorded"}},"kind":"create","recording":{"actor":"human:timo","causation":"cmd-child-ad5bb48ece8bbb9d560ff9a5fae58a028971bd037819cb61f2070e9d21b49f9e","correlation":"protocol-artifact-new","record_id":"aep.applied:child-ad5bb48ece8bbb9d560ff9a5fae58a028971bd037819cb61f2070e9d21b49f9e@1~b7b6a1833